      "writtenOn": "2023-04-21T23:01:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since `b` is not available to platform, WDYT about not having a platform variant of this library at all and always building this library in the context of an apex?\n\nOtherwise, `b build //b --config\u003dandroid` might not compile if we link it against stubs. You are right, Soong makes the platform variant of `b` link against impl of `a`, but that seems like an api boundary violation.",
      "parentUuid": "f1c935db_fd7e2236",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 583,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 584,
        "endChar": 96
      },
      "revId": "d6810e57fbc6245f360a9c23bd3575aeddd5710b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b998efe8_c9759892",
        "filename": "bp2build/cc_library_shared_conversion_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 668,
      "author": {
        "id": 1687194
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-21T21:13:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Trying to reason through the logic:\n\nMy understanding is that currently in Soong we\u0027d get something like:\n\nif bar and foo have the same min sdk version:\n\n```\n        \"//build/bazel/rules/apex:android-in_apexbar\": [\n            \"@api_surfaces//module-libapi/current:libplatform_stable\",\n            \"@api_surfaces//module-libapi/current:libapexfoo_stable\",\n        ],\n        \"//build/bazel/rules/apex:android-in_apexfoo\": [\n            \"@api_surfaces//module-libapi/current:libplatform_stable\",\n            \"@api_surfaces//module-libapi/current:libapexfoo_stable\",\n        ],\n        \"//build/bazel/rules/apex:android-non_apex\": [\n            \"@api_surfaces//module-libapi/current:libplatform_stable\",\n            \"@api_surfaces//module-libapi/current:libapexfoo_stable\",\n        ],\n ```\n        \n if bar and foo have different min sdk versions:\n \n ```\n        \"//build/bazel/rules/apex:android-in_apexbar\": [\n            \"@api_surfaces//module-libapi/current:libplatform_stable\",\n            \"@api_surfaces//module-libapi/current:libapexfoo_stable\",\n        ],\n        \"//build/bazel/rules/apex:android-in_apexfoo\": [\n            \"@api_surfaces//module-libapi/current:libplatform_stable\",\n            \":libapexfoo_stable\",\n        ],\n        \"//build/bazel/rules/apex:android-non_apex\": [\n            \"@api_surfaces//module-libapi/current:libplatform_stable\",\n            \"@api_surfaces//module-libapi/current:libapexfoo_stable\",\n        ],\n```\n\n\nI think the current logic for apexes is reasonable and valid, if verbose. We may need to evaluate the change to the platform logic a bit more as it seems like it\u0027ll introduce some discrepancies similar to the errors we\u0027ve been seeing currently.\n\nTo help reduce the BUILD file overhead, we could also consider migrating this as (doesn\u0027t have to be now, let\u0027s file a bug to evaluate):\n\n```\n        \"//build/bazel/platforms/os:android\": [\n            \"@api_surfaces//module-libapi/current:libplatform_stable\",\n            \"@api_surfaces//module-libapi/current:libapexfoo_stable\",\n        ],\n```\n\nAt least in the cases of APEXes, there shouldn\u0027t be a different API available to this library for its deps since it has to successfully link against the stubs when in apex configuration and there is no longer an apex name specific defines in compilation.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 657,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 668,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "d6810e57fbc6245f360a9c23bd3575aeddd5710b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
